WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:02.980
The Avengers are assembling yet again.

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:07.500
Speaking with ComicBook.com's Brandon Davis
during Spider-Man: Far From Home's London

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:12.450
press junket, Marvel Studios head Kevin Feige
revealed that Avengers: Endgame is returning

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:15.710
to theaters with extra footage and "a few
surprises."

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:20.119
At the time, Feige noted that he was unaware
if the rerelease had been announced, and seemed

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:22.980
to hint that he wasn't sure how much new footage
would be included.

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:27.470
What he was certain of was the most important
takeaway: Marvel is definitely bringing more

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:29.200
Endgame goodness to cinemas.

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:33.420
Feige shared additional details about the
rerelease in an interview with Screen Rant,

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:35.680
explaining that it isn't an extended cut.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:36.220
Instead:

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:40.250
"There will be a version going into theaters
with a bit of a marketing push with a few

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:41.680
new things at the end of the movie.

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:45.840
If you stay and watch the movie, after the
credits, there’ll be a deleted scene, a

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:47.780
little tribute, and a few surprises."

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:52.890
What these post-credits surprises could be
is anyone's guess, though we have a few ideas.

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:57.390
Perhaps Marvel finally decided to let the
entire world see the video of Ant-Man franchise

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:02.180
actors Paul Rudd and Michael Peña recapping
the events of the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:04.860
"Here's the deal, just give me the facts,
okay?"

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:05.800
"Only the facts, okay."

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:07.620
"Breathe, focus.

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:09.180
Keep it simple."

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:10.660
"No doubt, no doubt."

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:15.590
Maybe the surprises will be bloopers, or a
clip of Feige sitting down with notoriously

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:20.710
loose-lipped stars Mark Ruffalo and Tom Holland
and giving them a lecture about spoiling movies.

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:25.370
It could even be a special message from the
massive cast thanking Marvel fans for joining

00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:28.740
them on the cinematic journey that began back
in 2008.

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:33.460
The "little tribute" that Feige mentioned
is likely one honoring the late Stan Lee,

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:37.300
and there probably won't be a dry eye in the
house after it plays out on screen.

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:42.410
The re-release is scheduled to hit theaters
Friday, June 28, and could be either a one-night-only

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:47.360
engagement or finish its second run in cinemas
by end of day on Sunday, June 30.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:49.360
Why such a short time in theaters?

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:54.580
Marvel has another movie to roll out just
a few days later: Spider-Man: Far From Home,

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:59.170
the much-anticipated Spidey sequel that serves
as the official conclusion to Phase 3 of the

00:01:59.170 --> 00:01:59.760
MCU.

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:05.380
Far From Home debuts Tuesday, July 2 — only
a handful of days after Marvel is putting

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:07.060
Endgame back on the big screen.

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:11.560
Bringing the $2-billion-plus-earning superhero
ensemble to theaters for another round of

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:16.160
showings is one thing, but keeping it there
for an extended period of time is another.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:20.840
If the Endgame rerelease carried on into the
week of Far From Home's premiere, it could

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:23.080
impact the film's box office performance.

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:27.440
Marvel is a smarter company than that, and
wouldn't risk negatively affecting Far From

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:30.980
Home's success just so Avengers could rake
in some extra cash.

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:33.200
"All right, skedaddle there, young buck!"

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:34.240
"Thank you, Mr. Stark!

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:35.440
Thank you!"

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:41.220
On the topic of big box office bucks, it appears
that Marvel's main motivation for the Avengers:

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:43.920
Endgame rerelease is lifting the numbers a
bit.

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:48.820
Many watched carefully as Endgame inched closer
to making history as the top-earning movie

00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:53.640
in history by unseating James Cameron's Avatar,
but fans didn't see that happen before the

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:55.380
film ended its theatrical run.

00:02:55.910 --> 00:03:02.340
Though Avengers: Endgame took in $2.743 billion
worldwide, it still sits several million dollars

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:06.300
behind Avatar, which has earned $2.787 billion
globally.

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:10.180
All that stands between Avengers: Endgame
and the title of "Highest Grossing Film in

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:13.040
History" is roughly $44 million.

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:18.360
Endgame made $60 million during Thursday-night
domestic preview screenings alone, so it might

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:22.739
not be that difficult for the movie to rake
in that $44 million or so with a re-release.

00:03:22.739 --> 00:03:26.220
Be sure to check back with us soon for an
official update on how long you'll have to

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:28.200
see Avengers: Endgame in theaters again.

